/-!
# The exceptional divisor of the blowup in the ideal of denominators

Let `X` be a scheme, `L` an invertible `𝒪_X`-module and `s` a meromorphic section of `L`, let
`b : X' ⟶ X` be the blowup of `X` in the ideal of denominators of `s` and let `E ⊆ X'` be the
exceptional divisor.  This file proves that every local section of the ideal sheaf of `E` is a
denominator of the pulled back section `b^* s`, i.e. that

`ℐ_E · b^* s ⊆ b^* L`.

This is the content that the proof of [Stacks, Tag 0ESL] extracts from its computation on the
affine blowup charts: there `s = a'/a` over `Spec A`, the ideal of denominators is
`I = {x ∈ A | x a' ∈ a A}`, the chart is `Spec A[I/x]` with `E` cut out by `x`, and `x a' = a a''`
exhibits `x · b^* s` as the regular function `a''`.  The argument below replaces that computation
by a global one: a denominator pulls back to a denominator, the exceptional ideal on a chart is
generated by pullbacks of denominators, and being a denominator is a local condition.

It then turns that inclusion into a morphism of sheaves of modules `ℐ_E ⟶ b^* L`, proves it
monic, identifies `Hom(ℐ_E, b^* L)` with `b^* L ⊗ 𝒪_{X'}(E)` and so reads the morphism as a
global section `t` of `b^* L ⊗ 𝒪_{X'}(E)`.  That section is the one whose zero scheme the second
assertion of [Stacks, Tag 0ESL] calls `D`; the assertion itself is proved in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Blowup/DenominatorExceptionalDivisor.lean`, and the implementation
notes below say what it takes.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.DenominatorBlowup.denominators`: the denominators of a meromorphic section over an open
  set, as an ideal of the ring of sections there.
* `Stacks.DenominatorBlowup.exceptionalSheaf` and `exceptionalι`: the ideal sheaf `ℐ_E` of the
  exceptional divisor as a sheaf of `𝒪_{X'}`-modules, and its inclusion in the structure sheaf.
* `Stacks.DenominatorBlowup.exceptionalToDenominatorIdeal` and `exceptionalToPullL`: **the
  morphism `ℐ_E ⟶ b^* L`**, factored through the denominator ideal of `b^* s`.
* `Stacks.DenominatorBlowup.exceptionalTwist`: `𝒪_{X'}(E)`, the dual of `ℐ_E`.
* `Stacks.DenominatorBlowup.pullLTensorExceptionalTwistIso`: **the identification
  `b^* L ⊗ 𝒪_{X'}(E) ≅ Hom(ℐ_E, b^* L)`**.
* `Stacks.DenominatorBlowup.exceptionalHomSection` and `exceptionalTensorSection`: the morphism
  `ℐ_E ⟶ b^* L` read as a global section of `Hom(ℐ_E, b^* L)`, and then — through that
  identification — as **the global section `t` of `b^* L ⊗ 𝒪_{X'}(E)`**.

## Main results

* `Stacks.DenominatorBlowup.res_mem_denominators`: denominators restrict.
* `Stacks.DenominatorBlowup.mem_denominators_of_cover`: being a denominator is a local condition.
  This rests on the fact that the denominator ideal of a meromorphic section of an invertible
  sheaf embeds in the structure sheaf, so that local preimages are unique and therefore glue.
* `Stacks.DenominatorBlowup.isSectionOver_sectionOpens`: **the open subscheme `U` of
  [Stacks, Tag 0ESL] is a maximum, not merely a supremum** — `s` really does correspond to a
  section of `L` over `U`.
* `Stacks.DenominatorBlowup.app_mem_denominators`: **the pullback of a denominator is a
  denominator**, for any morphism of schemes along which pullbacks of meromorphic functions are
  defined ([Stacks, Tag 02OT]).
* `Stacks.DenominatorBlowup.ideal_exceptional_le_denominators`: on an affine open of the blowup
  lying over an affine open of `X`, the exceptional ideal is contained in the denominators of
  `b^* s`.
* `Stacks.DenominatorBlowup.mem_denominators_of_subschemeι_app_eq_zero`: **the global statement**
  — over an arbitrary open set of the blowup, every section of the ideal sheaf of the exceptional
  divisor is a denominator of `b^* s`.
* `Stacks.DenominatorBlowup.mono_exceptionalToPullL`: **the morphism `ℐ_E ⟶ b^* L` is a
  monomorphism**, for a regular meromorphic section `s`.
* `Stacks.DenominatorBlowup.exceptionalToPullL_comp_toK`: **the morphism `ℐ_E ⟶ b^* L` is
  multiplication by `b^* s`** — composed with `b^* L ⟶ 𝒦_{X'}(b^* L)` it is the ideal inclusion
  `ℐ_E ⟶ 𝒪_{X'}` followed by multiplication by `b^* s`.  This is the multiplied-out form of the
  section-matching clause of the second assertion; see the implementation notes.
* `Stacks.DenominatorBlowup.isIso_tensorDualToSheafHom_exceptional`: the rank-one map
  `b^* L ⊗ 𝒪_{X'}(E) ⟶ Hom(ℐ_E, b^* L)` is an isomorphism, which is what makes
  `pullLTensorExceptionalTwistIso` available.
* `Stacks.DenominatorBlowup.stacksIsInvertible_pullLTensorExceptionalTwist`:
  `b^* L ⊗ 𝒪_{X'}(E)` is invertible, so that the zero scheme of `t` can be formed at all.

## Implementation notes

The blowup used is `AlgebraicGeometry.blowUp`, the relative `Proj` of the Rees algebra sheaf,
because that is the one for which [Stacks, Tag 0809] is available here
(`AlgebraicGeometry.pullbacksMeromorphicSections_blowUpToBase`) and for which the exceptional
divisor is known to be an effective Cartier divisor
(`Stacks.Blowup.isEffectiveCartierDivisor_exceptionalIdeal`).  The admissibility statement of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Blowup/DenominatorAdmissible.lean` is stated for
`Stacks.Blowup.blowUp`; the two are isomorphic over `X` by
`AlgebraicGeometry.blowUpIso_hom_blowUpToBase`.

The key input, `app_mem_denominators`, is
`AlgebraicGeometry.smul_pullbackMeromorphicSection_valOver` read through the denominator rule of
[Stacks, Tag 02P0]: a denominator `c` of `t` over `V` is exactly a section with `c · t` in the
image of `N ⟶ 𝒦(N)`, and that lemma says the pullback of such a normal form is again one.

**How the morphism `ℐ_E ⟶ b^* L` is built, and why it is not written out sectionwise.** The
denominator ideal of [Stacks, Tag 02P0] is a *fibre product*
(`Stacks.DenominatorIdeal.denominatorIdeal`) of multiplication by `b^* s` and of the canonical
map `b^* L ⟶ 𝒦_{X'}(b^* L)`, and its second projection `denominatorIdealMul` is already
multiplication by `b^* s` with values in `b^* L`. So all that is constructed here is the
inclusion `ℐ_E ⟶ ` denominator ideal, and `exceptionalToPullL` is that composed with the
projection. The inclusion is the one hand-built `PresheafOfModules.Hom` of the file: on sections
over an open `W` it sends `y` to the unique preimage of `y` under the first projection, which
exists because `y` is a denominator
(`Stacks.DenominatorBlowup.mem_denominators_of_subschemeι_app_eq_zero`) and is unique because
that projection is a monomorphism for an invertible sheaf
(`Stacks.DenominatorIdealInvertible.denominatorIdeal_inclusion_mono`). Additivity, linearity and
naturality are then all the same one-line argument: both sides have the same image under an
injective map.

Two conveniences follow from going through the fibre product rather than straight to `b^* L`.
Monicity is `CategoryTheory.mono_of_mono_fac` against the kernel inclusion `ℐ_E ⟶ 𝒪_{X'}`,
followed by [Stacks, Tag 02P0]'s `denominatorIdeal_section_mono`; and the section-matching
identity `exceptionalToPullL_comp_toK` is the commuting square of the fibre product, so it needs
no computation at all.

**The identification `Hom(ℐ_E, b^* L) ≅ b^* L ⊗ 𝒪_{X'}(E)`** is
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.isIso_tensorDualToSheafHom`, the rank-one map of [Stacks, Tag 08JJ]
step (5), at `E := ℐ_E` and `F := b^* L`. Its hypothesis is a finite dual basis for `ℐ_E` on a
covering family, and `ℐ_E` has rank-*one* bases there: `E` is an effective Cartier divisor
(`Stacks.Blowup.isEffectiveCartierDivisor_exceptionalIdeal`), so `ℐ_E` is invertible, hence
locally trivial ([Stacks, Tag 0B8M], `Stacks.InvertibleRankOneScheme`), and a trivialization is a
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.DualBasisOne`. The only glue added here is
`Stacks.DenominatorBlowup.finiteDualBasisOfDualBasisOne`, which reads a rank-one basis as a
finite one on the one-element index type. No associator or unitor is used: the dual
`𝒪_{X'}(E) = Hom(ℐ_E, 𝒪_{X'})` is the *second* tensor factor on the nose in the statement of the
rank-one map, so the untwisting `𝒪_{X'}(E) ⊗ ℐ_E ≅ 𝒪_{X'}` never has to be threaded through a
reassociation.

**The section-matching clause is stated in multiplied-out form.** The second assertion of
[Stacks, Tag 0ESL] asks that `b^* s` correspond, via `b^* L ≅ 𝒪_{X'}(D - E)`, to the meromorphic
section `1_D ⊗ (1_E)^{-1}`. The literal expression `1_D ⊗ (1_E)^{-1}` cannot be formed in this
development: nothing here constructs the *inverse* of a regular section inside the sheaf of
meromorphic sections, and the tensor product of meromorphic sections of [Stacks, Tag 02SL] —
which is what would multiply `1_D` by it — is available only under `[IsIntegral X]`, a
hypothesis Tag 0ESL does not carry and which the blowup of a locally Noetherian scheme need not
satisfy. What is proved instead is the identity the source's own proof uses, namely that
`b^* s` *is* the fraction whose numerator is the morphism `ℐ_E ⟶ b^* L` and whose denominator is
the ideal inclusion: `Stacks.DenominatorBlowup.exceptionalToPullL_comp_toK` says

`(ℐ_E ⟶ b^* L) ≫ (b^* L ⟶ 𝒦_{X'}(b^* L)) = (ℐ_E ⟶ 𝒪_{X'}) ≫ (multiplication by b^* s)`,

which is the equation `1_D ⊗ (1_E)^{-1} = b^* s` with both sides multiplied by `1_E`. It is
equivalent to the clause once `1_E` is invertible in the sheaf of meromorphic sections, and it is
a statement about `b^* s` and the two named morphisms only, so it is checkable without that
inverse.

**Where the second assertion is finished.** The global section `t` of `b^* L ⊗ 𝒪_{X'}(E)` is
here (`Stacks.DenominatorBlowup.exceptionalTensorSection`), and so is the invertibility of
`b^* L ⊗ 𝒪_{X'}(E)` that forming its zero scheme requires. The remaining step is that `t` is a
*regular* section in the sense of `AlgebraicGeometry.IsRegularSection`, i.e. that multiplication
by `t` is a monomorphism `𝒪_{X'} ⟶ b^* L ⊗ 𝒪_{X'}(E)`. What is proved here is the neighbouring
statement that the morphism `ℐ_E ⟶ b^* L` is a monomorphism
(`Stacks.DenominatorBlowup.mono_exceptionalToPullL`); passing from it to regularity of `t` means
transporting monicity across the adjunction `Hom(𝒪, Hom(ℐ_E, b^* L)) ≅ Hom(ℐ_E, b^* L)` of
[Stacks, Tag 03EO]. That transport is
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.mono_unitHomEquiv_symm_homSections` of
`StacksFrontier/Algebra/Category/ModuleCat/Sheaf/SheafHomRegularSection.lean`, proved for an
arbitrary ringed site, and
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Blowup/DenominatorExceptionalDivisor.lean` applies it here and
finishes the assertion: `D := zeroScheme t` is an effective Cartier divisor by
`AlgebraicGeometry.isEffectiveCartierDivisor_zeroScheme_iff_isRegularSection`, [Stacks, Tag 01X0]
(`AlgebraicGeometry.existsUnique_invertibleSheafIso_zeroScheme`) gives the unique isomorphism
`𝒪_{X'}(D) ≅ b^* L ⊗ 𝒪_{X'}(E)` carrying `1_D` to `t`, and untwisting by
`Stacks.Divisors.invertibleSheafPairing` for `E` turns that into `b^* L ≅ 𝒪_{X'}(D - E)`. The
rank-one dual bases that the transport needs are the ones
`Stacks.DenominatorBlowup.exists_coversTop_dualBasisOne_exceptionalSheaf` produces below.

